  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The 2026 Pittsburgh St. Patrick’s Day Parade, one of the nation's largest and oldest (dating to 1869), is held in downtown Pittsburgh on the Saturday before St. Patrick’s Day, starting at 10 a.m.. The 1.4-mile parade typically features over 200 units, including marching bands, Irish dance groups, and over 200,000 spectators. Parade Details (Saturday, March 14, 2026): Time: Starts at 10:00 AM. Route: Begins at the intersection of Liberty Avenue and 11th Street, moves along Grant Street, and turns right onto the Boulevard of the Allies, ending at Commonwealth Place. Highlights: Irish step dancers, military members, floats, and community organizations. Celebration: The event is accompanied by a massive city-wide celebration, including a parade day dash (5K/1-mile). Tips for Attendees: Parking: Downtown parking is available at facilities like The Pennsylvanian Upper Lot, Liberty Center/Westin Convention Center Garage, and PPG Paints Arena South Lot. Safety: Police advise vigilance; streets along the route begin closing early, with parking restrictions usually starting Friday night, according to WTAE. Alternative Activities: A 5K and 1-mile fun run are held before the parade at 8 AM, as noted by P3R.org. Note: The 2026 parade took place on March 14th.",
